---
import { graphStart } from '../../lib/explainers/graph-model.mjs';
import { graphResult } from './graph-render.mjs';
---
<graph-traversal class="lab wide graph-lab" aria-label="Find callers of a failed service">
  <div class="lab-heading"><span class="eyebrow">Interactive experiment</span></div>
  <h3>How far does the dependency reach?</h3>
  <div class="lab-introduction">
    <p>Eight services call one another. An arrow points from the caller to its dependency. Inventory has failed; the query walks incoming calls to find services that depend on it, directly or indirectly. A solid call is required; a dashed call is optional and has a fallback.</p>
    <p class="try-this">Choose <strong>Advance one layer</strong> twice to find Inventory's direct callers, then their callers. Disable <strong>Required calls only</strong> to include Email and Reports. Add shared calls to see more relationships examined, including routes to services already found. Set the hop limit to 1: the result names the frontier left unexpanded. Choose Warehouse and four hops to see a traversal exhaust its frontier instead. Every query change starts a fresh traversal.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="lab-controls">
    <p class="lab-area-label">Controls</p>
    <div class="control-line"><label>Failed service <select data-start><option value="inventory">Inventory</option><option value="checkout">Checkout</option><option value="warehouse">Warehouse</option></select></label><label>Maximum hops <select data-limit>{[1,2,3,4].map(n => <option value={n} selected={n === 3}>{n}</option>)}</select></label></div>
    <div class="control-line"><label class="check-label"><input data-required type="checkbox" checked /> Required calls only</label><label class="check-label"><input data-dense type="checkbox" /> Add shared calls</label></div>
    <div class="control-line"><button data-next>Advance one layer</button><button data-reset>Reset traversal</button></div>
  </div>
  <div class="lab-output paper-surface">
    <p class="lab-area-label">Result <span>Relationships inspected and services found are counted separately</span></p>
    <div data-view set:html={graphResult(graphStart())}></div>
    <p data-status role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true">Inventory found. Ready to expand incoming calls.</p>
  </div>
  <details class="model-note"><summary>What this model leaves out</summary><p>This is breadth-first reachability on a fixed eight-node graph, using incoming adjacency lists and a global visited set. Each click expands one frontier, counts each inspected incoming relationship, applies the optional-call filter, and queues each newly found service once. The start node is excluded from matches. It retains one shortest path per endpoint and does not enumerate all paths or reproduce Cypher's default relationship-reuse semantics. The hop limit bounds the query. Calls are invented static dependencies, not observed failures; retries, caches, replicas, request traffic, and partial outages are absent. Counts show algorithmic work in this model, not measured engine performance.</p></details>
  <noscript><p>With required calls only, one hop from Inventory finds Checkout and Warehouse. Two hops add Storefront and Returns; three add Admin. Optional calls also reach Email and Reports. A visited set stops the Warehouse–Returns cycle from creating repeated matches.</p></noscript>
</graph-traversal>
<script>
  import { graphStart, graphStep } from '../../lib/explainers/graph-model.mjs';
  import { graphResult, graphName, graphProgress } from './graph-render.mjs';
  class GraphTraversal extends HTMLElement {
    connectedCallback() {
      if (this.dataset.ready) return;
      this.dataset.ready = 'true';
      const start = this.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-start]')!;
      const limit = this.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-limit]')!;
      const required = this.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('[data-required]')!;
      const dense = this.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('[data-dense]')!;
      const next = this.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-next]')!;
      let state = graphStart();
      const render = () => {
        this.querySelector('[data-view]')!.innerHTML = graphResult(state);
        next.disabled = state.done;
        this.querySelector('[data-status]')!.textContent = `${graphName(state.start)}: ${state.depth} ${state.depth===1?'layer':'layers'} expanded, ${state.inspected.length} ${state.inspected.length===1?'relationship':'relationships'} examined, ${state.visited.length-1} ${state.visited.length===2?'service':'services'} found. ${graphProgress(state)}`;
      };
      const reset = () => { state = graphStart({start: start.value, limit: Number(limit.value), dense: dense.checked, requiredOnly: required.checked}); render(); };
      for (const control of [start, limit, required, dense]) control.addEventListener('change', reset);
      next.addEventListener('click', () => { state = graphStep(state); render(); });
      this.querySelector('[data-reset]')!.addEventListener('click', reset);
      reset();
    }
  }
  if (!customElements.get('graph-traversal')) customElements.define('graph-traversal', GraphTraversal);
</script>
